# Generated files. Two computers scanning around the same time both rewrite
# these, and git cannot merge them meaningfully — the text is derived, so a
# three-way merge produces a document that matches neither machine's data.
#
# `union` keeps both sides rather than leaving conflict markers, which is still
# wrong as a document but never blocks the pull. The actual resolution is always
# the same: run `python3 update.py --combine-only` afterwards and they are
# rebuilt from the machine folders, which DO merge cleanly because each computer
# only ever writes its own.
ALL-COMPUTERS.json  merge=union
BY-COMPUTER.md      merge=union
BY-ACCOUNT.md       merge=union
BY-COMPANY.md       merge=union
README.md           merge=union
